===JSON_START===
{"verdict": {"body": {"ko": "엔케이젠바이오텍코리아는 2025년 3분기와 2026년 2분기 분기 손익이 흑자로 전환했고 연간 영업손실 폭도 다년간 축소돼 왔으나, 연간 매출은 2023년부터 2025년까지 3년 연속 줄었고 분기 손익의 변동성도 여전히 크다. 재무구조는 2025년 하반기 감자·유상증자를 거쳐 부채비율이 정상 범위로 복귀했지만 영업활동 현금흐름은 계속 마이너스를 기록하고 있다. 최대주주는 미국 OTC 시장의 NKGen Biotech, Inc.로, 모회사의 임상 파이프라인 진행 상황과 한국법인의 상업화 매출 간 연결고리는 아직 명확히 확인되지 않는다. 가장 중요한 변수는 과거 회계감사의견 관련 상장폐지 사유에서 비롯된 매매거래 정지 상태의 해소 여부로, 2026년 봄까지도 거래정지가 이어진 것으로 보도됐다. 다음 분기 보고서의 손익 추이와 거래소의 상장적격성 후속 결정이 함께 확인돼야 전체 그림을 판단할 수 있다. 이 리포트는 사실관계와 앞으로 확인이 필요한 지점을 정리한 것이며, 이에 대한 판단은 독자 각자의 몫이다.", "en": "NKGen Biotech Korea swung to quarterly profit in the third quarter of 2025 and the second quarter of 2026, and its annual operating loss has narrowed over several years, yet annual revenue declined for three consecutive years from 2023 through 2025 and quarterly earnings volatility remains high. The balance sheet returned to a more normal debt-to-equity range after a capital reduction and rights offering in the second half of 2025, but operating cash flow has continued to run negative. The controlling shareholder is NKGen Biotech, Inc., listed on the U.S. OTC market, and the link between the parent's clinical pipeline progress and the Korean entity's commercialized revenue has not yet been clearly established. The most important variable is whether the trading halt stemming from a past audit-opinion-related delisting trigger is resolved, as reports as of spring 2026 still described the stock as halted. Both the earnings trend in the next quarterly report and any follow-up exchange decision on listing eligibility need to be checked together to form a complete picture. This report lays out the facts and the points that still need to be confirmed; the resulting judgment rests with each reader."}}}
===JSON_END===

106190-fbcd8f01f30143c50bd68226.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "The Chungju plant secured EU GMP approval in 2024 and US FDA approval in 2025, establishing a system capable of supplying carbapenem-class antibiotic APIs to global regulated markets. The company defines its carbapenem concentration as a competitive advantage that is not easily replicated, citing the GMP regulatory structure that prohibits cross-production with other antibiotics at the same facility. As listed companies exporting carbapenem APIs domestically are rare, new competitor entry requires considerable time and certification costs.", "1": "The company turned from an operating loss of KRW 1.1 billion in Q1 2026 to an operating profit of KRW 6.29 billion in Q2, up 95.6% year-over-year. Net income attributable to controlling shareholders also swung from a net loss in Q1 to KRW 5.25 billion in Q2, up 124.0% year-over-year. The company attributed the Q1 loss to temporary costs such as facility maintenance, making it a key point to monitor whether this factor recurs in the following quarter.", "2": "The debt-to-equity ratio steadily declined from 32.3% in 2022 to 10.0% in 2025, while operating cash flow turned from -KRW 3.7 billion to KRW 17.0 billion over the same period, expanding in the process. Total equity at the end of 2025 increased to KRW 130.7 billion, reflecting greater financial buffer capacity. Compared to earnings volatility, cash generation has shown a relatively stable trend.", "3": "As of 2025, 87.4% of revenue came from sales to the largest shareholder, ACS Dobfar, and Europe accounted for 87% of sales by region. The high dependence on a single customer and region means that changes in demand or policy at that client could directly impact performance. While the company describes this as a competitive strength, the industry points to whether this concentration eases as a key variable.", "4": "The decline in 2025 performance was attributed to price dumping by Chinese competitors and raw material supply instability caused by an explosion accident at an overseas intermediate material supplier. In addition, a production gap of about 40 days at year-end occurred during facility investment at the Chungju and Daeso synthesis plants, adding to profitability pressure. If external supply chain risks materialize again, they could lead to further production disruptions.", "5": "Revenue in Q4 2025 fell to KRW 14.0 billion, and Q1 2026 recorded an operating loss of KRW 1.1 billion, showing significant quarter-to-quarter volatility. Annual revenue also declined from KRW 102.9 billion in 2022 to KRW 70.2 billion in 2025, so further quarterly confirmation is needed to determine whether the rebound from the bottom will continue. Quarterly profits are structurally sensitive to one-off costs and production schedules.", "6": "As most of the revenue is concentrated on supply to the largest shareholder, ACS Dobfar, and to Europe, changes in that client's purchasing policy or in the European regulatory environment could directly affect performance. Customer diversification is underway, but it is structurally difficult for the concentration to change significantly in the short term.", "7": "In 2025, raw material supply became unstable due to an explosion accident at an overseas intermediate material supplier, and if a similar supply chain shock recurs, production could be affected again. Temporary production gaps due to facility investment have also occurred in the past.", "8": "Price competition and dumping by Chinese companies have been cited as a factor in the 2025 earnings slowdown, so pricing pressure on APIs persists. As sales are virtually entirely export-based, the company is also affected by fluctuations in the KRW exchange rate."}
===JSON_END===

032800-4aa1e41405450bb9886e5c3c.text:
===JSON_START===
{"verdict": {"body": {"ko": "판타지오는 2026년 SBS '김부장' 흥행으로 매니지먼트 중심 기업에서 종합 콘텐츠 제작사로 체질을 바꾸려는 시도가 가시적 성과를 낸 해였다. 그러나 2025년까지 공시된 실적을 보면 매출은 전년 대비 47.2% 줄고 영업손실과 지배주주 순손실이 모두 전년보다 확대되며, 2023년부터 2025년까지 3년 연속 영업적자, 2022년부터 2025년까지 4년 연속 지배주주 순손실이라는 구조적 수익성 과제가 남아 있다. 여기에 소속 핵심 배우 두 명의 탈세 의혹과 그에 따른 회사 차원의 공식 사과, 짧은 기간에 이어진 80% 무상감자와 복수의 유상증자, 최대주주 교체 등은 재무·지배구조 측면의 불확실성을 더하는 요인이다. 반면 2025년 영업활동 현금흐름이 127억원으로 개선된 점, 일일드라마와 공동제작 신작으로 제작 라인업을 넓히고 있는 점은 균형 잡힌 평가를 위해 함께 살펴야 할 긍정적 신호다. 결국 이 회사의 다음 국면은 신작들의 흥행 여부와 반복된 자본 조달이 실제 수익성 개선으로 이어지는지에 달려 있으며, 투자자는 다가오는 분기보고서와 작품별 편성·방영 공시를 통해 이를 확인해야 한다. 이 보고서는 공시된 사실과 보도된 정보를 바탕으로 작성됐다.", "en": "For Fantagio, 2026 was a year in which the success of SBS's 'Manager Kim' produced visible results in its effort to shift from a management-centered company toward a comprehensive content producer. Yet the disclosed results through 2025 show revenue down 47.2% year over year with both the operating loss and controlling-interest net loss widening from the prior year, leaving the structural profitability challenge of three consecutive years of operating losses from 2023 through 2025 and four consecutive years of controlling-interest net losses from 2022 through 2025 unresolved. Adding to the uncertainty are tax evasion allegations against two of the company's core actors and the resulting corporate apology, along with an 80% capital reduction and multiple share issuances compressed into a short period, plus a change in the largest shareholder, all of which add to financial and governance-related uncertainty. On the other side of the ledger, the improvement in 2025 operating cash flow to KRW 12.7 billion and the expansion of the production lineup into daily dramas and new co-productions are positive signals that deserve equal weight in a balanced assessment. Ultimately, the company's next phase will hinge on whether its upcoming titles succeed commercially and whether repeated capital raises translate into actual profitability gains, points investors should verify through upcoming quarterly reports and title-by-title broadcast disclosures. This report is based on disclosed facts and reported information."}}}
===JSON_END===

