376180-13ca314fb74c4e597a081158.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "The company recorded operating profit surpluses for two consecutive quarters in Q1 and Q2 2026, showing signs of emerging from the loss phase of 2025. Q2 operating profit was KRW 1.2 billion, up 3,714.2% quarter-on-quarter and 139.2% year-on-year. Reduction in selling, general and administrative expenses was cited as the main factor behind the profitability improvement.", "1": "In May 2026, the company established PICOGRAM USA in California to secure a North American distribution and marketing base. It also built a royalty revenue structure through a carbon block facility and technology export contract with China's Kenature. The company is positioned to benefit from the industry trend in which expanding overseas operations by downstream water purifier manufacturers lead to increased demand for components.", "2": "In addition to its existing water purifier and filter business, the company is expanding its revenue sources into carbon block materials, food waste disposers, and cosmetics brand 'Celine Stem'. It also plans to invest in expanding production capacity during 2026 to respond to demand for conversion to carbon block driven by rising activated carbon prices. The geographic scope of new businesses is also widening, including expansion of the cosmetics distribution network into Vietnam and North America.", "3": "2025 revenue was KRW 30.9 billion, down 4.0% year-on-year, while operating loss of KRW 704 million and controlling shareholders' net loss of KRW 1.1 billion both turned to deficits. Increased selling, general and administrative expenses, including advertising costs for new product launch promotions, had an impact. Losses from early redemption of convertible bonds and foreign exchange translation losses also contributed to the expanded net loss.", "4": "Q2 2026 revenue of KRW 8.44 billion increased 27.8% quarter-on-quarter but decreased 15.2% year-on-year. Quarterly revenue has remained significantly lower for three consecutive quarters since Q2 2025's KRW 9.94 billion. As the profit improvement is mainly attributable to cost reduction, the sustainability of this improvement may be put to the test if revenue itself does not recover accordingly.", "5": "The company itself stated in its semi-annual report that competitors hold an overwhelming share of the carbon block material market. The structure is such that securing new customers is not easy, as major water purifier manufacturers are already dominated by competitors. If the pace of market share expansion is slow amid continued new business investment, the results relative to costs could be delayed.", "6": "Over the past five quarters, operating profit has fluctuated widely, alternating between surpluses and deficits. Operating losses continued in Q3 and Q4 2025, with the loss expanding to KRW 1.05 billion in Q4. Given the large variance in quarterly performance, it is premature to conclude a trend reversal based solely on a single quarter's surplus.", "7": "Rising prices of carbon block raw materials such as activated carbon represent both an opportunity factor through conversion demand and a potential cost burden factor. Increased foreign exchange translation losses were reflected in the expanded net loss in 2025, suggesting that exposure to exchange rate fluctuations could grow as the share of overseas revenue and transactions increases. One-off expenses arising from financial structure management processes, such as the case of losses related to convertible bonds, are also a variable.", "8": "New businesses such as food waste disposers and cosmetics incurred cost burdens first due to expanded marketing investment in 2025. The operation of the North American subsidiary PICOGRAM USA and the expansion of the cosmetics distribution network in Vietnam are also at a stage requiring initial costs. The key to future profitability is when the revenue contribution from new businesses will exceed the scale of costs."}
===JSON_END===

310200-15a0ab6b4d1c57b40fcb5082.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "Aniplus and its merged subsidiary Animax each hold exclusive domestic distribution rights to proven hit Japanese anime IPs such as 'Demon Slayer' and 'Attack on Titan.' 'Demon Slayer: Infinity Castle' drew approximately 5.81 million moviegoers domestically, ranking as the all-time number-one Japanese film at the Korean box office, with global box office revenue reaching JPY 117.9 billion. Such large-scale IPs have a revenue structure that extends beyond theatrical earnings to OTT releases, re-releases, and merchandise sales.", "1": "The absorption-type merger of Animax, completed on July 1, 2026, established an integrated system spanning IP sourcing, broadcasting, theatrical distribution, and OTT distribution. The company stated that this merger would serve as an opportunity to enhance management efficiency, fully launch its in-house production business, and newly launch an online store and portal service. Operating as a single corporate entity while maintaining two broadcast channels may contribute to cost efficiency.", "2": "Operating cash flow surged significantly from KRW 21.2 billion in 2022 to KRW 85.6 billion in 2025, showing a clear improvement in cash-generating capacity relative to earnings volatility. This appears related to a business structure in which revenue from major box-office hits flows in as cash relatively quickly. Steady cash generation could serve as a funding source for securing new IP or investing in in-house production.", "3": "Quarterly results show significant volatility, with revenue and operating profit surging 94.7% and 437.8% quarter-on-quarter, respectively, in Q3 2025, before swinging to an operating loss of KRW 2.05 billion in Q4. Even after returning to profitability in Q1 2026, net income attributable to controlling shareholders in Q2 fell 56.3% quarter-on-quarter. A structure in which performance fluctuates sharply depending on the release timing of major theatrical distribution titles makes it difficult to identify quarterly trends.", "4": "The operating margin declined from 20.5% in 2023 to 15.1% in 2025, with operating profit and net income attributable to controlling shareholders in 2025 falling 9.8% and 22.8% year-on-year, respectively. The fact that the profit growth trend that continued through 2024 reversed in 2025 suggests a need to examine changes in cost structure or business mix.", "5": "The debt-to-equity ratio rose steadily each year, from 75.8% in 2022 to 97.4% in 2023, 106.4% in 2024, and 111.7% in 2025. As of the end of 2025, total liabilities stood at KRW 143.2 billion, exceeding total equity of KRW 128.2 billion. How the company manages its financial leverage level amid the merger and new business expansion could be a key point to watch.", "6": "The company's core revenue source is based on exclusive domestic distribution rights granted by Japanese anime IP holders. If competition for securing lineups of new IP intensifies or the terms for renewing licenses for major IPs become unfavorable, this could affect the revenue structure. A structure in which performance is heavily dependent on the box-office success of specific blockbuster titles indicates a high concentration of licensing.", "7": "The company has a history of raising mezzanine funding, such as convertible bonds, during its growth process, and the possibility of further equity dilution in the course of raising funds for new business investments or acquisitions in the future cannot be ruled out. The rising trend in the debt-to-equity ratio is also a point to watch from a financial structure perspective.", "8": "If comprehensive OTT platforms such as Netflix and TVING, as well as global anime-specialized platforms, expand their investment in anime content, this could put competitive pressure on Laftel's content exclusivity and subscriber base. If competition for content distribution rights intensifies among platforms, the cost of securing distribution rights could also rise."}
===JSON_END===

123040-72e62d787a66616d6b39aaa0.text:
