{"0": "In Q2 2026, operating profit was KRW 5.72 billion and net income attributable to controlling shareholders was KRW 5.96 billion, turning positive compared to the previous quarter. The reduction in operating loss from KRW 1.56 billion in Q1 2026 to a turnaround in Q2 suggests the possibility of cost structure improvement. However, given the precedent of alternating profits and losses over five consecutive quarters, it is premature to conclude this as a trend.", "1": "The debt ratio at the end of 2025 was 54.0%, down from 75.6% in 2024. Operating cash flow for the same year was KRW 30.6 billion, a significant increase from KRW 2.37 billion in 2024. This can be interpreted as expanded buffer capacity in terms of financial stability.", "2": "Following registration as a Tier 1 vendor for Stellantis in 2022, the opening of an ESS research center in 2024, and the establishment of a new subsidiary in 2025, the company has continued efforts to expand beyond its existing core electronic components business. Transaction history with global automakers such as GM has also been maintained over a long period.", "3": "After posting a large operating profit of KRW 19.6 billion in 2024, the company turned to an operating loss of KRW 3.16 billion in 2025. Net income attributable to controlling shareholders also reversed from KRW 20.3 billion in 2024 to a net loss of KRW 2.46 billion in 2025. There have been precedents where profit declined or turned into a loss even in years when revenue increased, indicating that revenue growth does not necessarily translate into profit improvement.", "4": "Over the five quarters from Q2 2025 to Q2 2026, operating profit alternated in the order of loss-profit-loss-loss-profit. Such volatility makes it difficult to predict the annual trend based on a single quarter's turnaround to profit. The sum of net income attributable to controlling shareholders over the most recent four quarters was KRW 9.87 billion, less than half of the annual profit in 2024 (KRW 20.3 billion).", "5": "In 2025, the Vietnam subsidiary was liquidated, and disclosures regarding capital reduction of subsidiaries and disposal of shares in other companies followed in succession. During this process of restructuring the overseas production network, the possibility of one-time costs or asset impairments cannot be ruled out. The final financial impact of the restructuring needs to be confirmed through future disclosures.", "6": "The company is known to have a structure with high revenue dependence on specific automakers such as GM. Changes in the production plans or new model launch schedules of major customers could directly affect Ecocap's sales and operating rate. The pace of customer diversification needs to be continuously monitored through future disclosures.", "7": "With production bases in China and Mexico, the company's earnings are exposed to exchange rate fluctuations such as KRW/USD and KRW/MXN. Fluctuations in raw material prices, such as copper, the main raw material for wires, can also affect costs. These external variables can be considered one of the factors that increase quarterly earnings volatility.", "8": "In August 2026, there was a correction disclosure regarding the semi-annual report (as of June 2026). The past instances of disclosure corrections related to capital reduction of subsidiaries and equity disposals illustrate the potential for changes in financial disclosures. Investors need to distinguish between confirmed figures in regular reports and preliminary figures."}
===JSON_END===

