{"verdict": {"body": {"ko": "파이버프로는 2022년 흑자 전환 이후 2025년까지 매출과 영업이익, 지배주주 순이익이 뚜렷한 회복·성장 경로를 보였으며, 2025년 영업이익률 23.3%는 해당 기간 중 가장 높은 수준이다. 다만 2026년 들어 분기별 영업이익이 1분기 47.6억원에서 2분기 27억원으로 줄어드는 등 개별 공급계약 시점에 따른 변동성이 여전히 크다는 점도 함께 확인된다. 국내 방산 고객에 더해 일본·미국 등 해외 고객과의 계약이 늘어나며 고객·지역 기반이 넓어지고 있는 점은 사업 구조의 변화로 주목할 만하다. 우주신기술 지정, 생산 능력 확충을 위한 부동산 취득, 기업가치 제고 계획 등은 중장기 사업 확장 의지를 보여주는 사실들이다. 2026년 3분기 이후 실적은 아직 정기보고서로 확정되지 않은 만큼, 다가오는 분기보고서 공시와 개별 계약의 이행 상황을 함께 지켜볼 필요가 있다. 이 보고서는 정보 제공을 목적으로 작성됐다.", "en": "Since turning profitable in 2022, Fiberpro has shown a clear recovery and growth path in revenue, operating profit, and net profit attributable to owners through 2025, with the 2025 operating margin of 23.3% the highest level within the disclosed period. At the same time, quarterly operating profit fell from KRW 4.76 billion in the first quarter of 2026 to KRW 2.7 billion in the second quarter, confirming that volatility tied to the timing of individual supply contracts remains significant. The expansion of contracts with overseas customers in Japan and the United States, in addition to domestic defense customers, is notable as a change in the company's business structure, broadening its customer and geographic base. The new space technology designation, the acquisition of real estate to expand production capacity, and the corporate value-up plan are all facts pointing to an intent to expand the business over the medium to long term. Because results from the third quarter of 2026 onward have not yet been confirmed through a formal quarterly report, the upcoming quarterly filing and the execution status of individual contracts both warrant continued attention. This report is provided for informational purposes only."}}}
===JSON_END===

131400-a010c0cc99bca4875067321b.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "In Q1 2026, operating profit was KRW 350 million, followed by KRW 1.51 billion in Q2, a 325.6% increase from the previous quarter, expanding the scale of profitability. Revenue also rose for two consecutive quarters in Q1 and Q2 2026 after bottoming out in Q4 2025, showing a trend of simultaneous improvement in top-line growth and profitability. Net income attributable to controlling interests also turned profitable for two consecutive quarters, showing a trend of narrowing losses.", "1": "In October 2026, the largest shareholder, Nexton&Roll Korea, participated in a third-party allotment capital increase worth KRW 5.5 billion, raising its stake to over 25%, with the stake including special related parties expanding to 28.13%. The raised funds are planned to be invested in building a production line for large-area FPCB of 1m or more, in response to the trend toward larger EV, battery, and ESS markets. The structure in which the largest shareholder repeatedly injects capital directly can be interpreted as a factor demonstrating stability in management control and a commitment to business expansion.", "2": "ProLogium of Taiwan, in which $8.5 million was invested in 2021, announced that it has begun mass production of 3.5th generation lithium ceramic all-solid-state batteries at its Taoyuan plant. ProLogium has also received investment from Mercedes-Benz, POSCO Holdings, and others, and aims to achieve mass production of 4th generation batteries by 2028 through its Dunkirk Gigafactory in France. If the commercialization of all-solid-state batteries gains momentum, interest may continue in the value of the equity stake held by EV Advanced Materials.", "3": "Net losses attributable to controlling interests continued for two consecutive years from 2024 to 2025, and in 2025 revenue also declined 28.0% year-over-year, resulting in a contraction in scale as well. Over the most recent four quarters (Q3 2025 to Q2 2026), cumulative net losses attributable to controlling interests of KRW 8.02 billion have accumulated, indicating that the turn to profitability in the most recent two quarters has not yet offset the overall annual loss structure. Given the large volatility in quarterly performance, it is necessary to verify the sustainability of the profitable trend every quarter.", "4": "Following the resolution in July 2026 for a 10-to-1 reverse stock split to cover accumulated deficits, in October an additional 1,177,884 new shares were issued combining a third-party allotment and a small-scale public offering. The new shares are scheduled to be listed on October 27, 2026, and since the small-scale public offering shares are not subject to mandatory holding periods, there is a possibility of increased trading volume immediately after listing. Repeated frequent capital increases and reverse stock splits reduce the comparability of per-share metrics and increase the burden on investors in tracking the capital structure.", "5": "Operating cash flow in 2025 was -KRW 3.49 billion, turning negative from the positive KRW 9.89 billion recorded in 2024. Amid the ongoing slowdown in EV market demand (chasm phase), changes in orders from downstream customers can directly affect revenue and profitability. Since the ProLogium investment asset is classified as a non-core business, the pace of profitability recovery in the core FPCB business itself remains a more important variable.", "6": "Annual operating profit/loss has frequently changed direction, repeating a pattern of loss-loss-profit-loss from 2022 to 2025. Quarterly results have also shown significant volatility, with losses widening in Q3 and Q4 2025 followed by a sharp turnaround to profitability in Q1 and Q2 2026. If there is high dependence on supply to a specific major customer, changes in that customer's orders can directly affect performance.", "7": "In 2026 alone, a series of events occurred in succession, including a 10-to-1 reverse stock split, a third-party allotment capital increase, and a small-scale public offering, causing significant short-term changes in capital and the number of shares issued. The rapid increase in the stake of the largest shareholder, Nexton&Roll Korea, from 17.3% to 28.13% (including special related parties) within a short period also demonstrates the speed of changes in governance structure. If additional fundraising or changes in equity stakes continue, it will be necessary to continuously monitor the possibility of dilution for existing shareholders.", "8": "The ProLogium equity stake is a strategic investment made in 2021 worth $8.5 million, and ProLogium's pursuit of a Nasdaq listing or its mass production schedule is entirely dependent on ProLogium's own business progress. Changes in the valuation of this equity stake have low direct relevance to the core FPCB business performance of EV Advanced Materials. As this is a minority equity investment in a foreign company, there is relatively greater uncertainty in information accessibility and valuation."}
===JSON_END===

