{"verdict": {"body": {"ko": "이지스는 2025년 매출 29.8% 감소와 영업손익 적자 전환에 이어 2026년 1·2분기까지 연속 영업손실을 기록하며 수익성 회복 과제를 안고 있다. 동시에 제주도 SaaS형 디지털 트윈 계약, 피지컬 AI·우주항공 신사업, 30억원 규모 자사주 취득·소각 등 사업·자본 양 측면에서 변화를 시도하고 있다. 부채비율은 낮아졌지만 영업활동 현금흐름은 순유출로 전환돼, 재무구조와 현금창출력 사이에 상반된 흐름이 동시에 나타나고 있다. 매출 구조상 공공기관 대상 구축 용역 의존도가 높아 분기별 변동성이 이어질 가능성이 있으며, SaaS 전환의 실제 성과는 아직 수치로 확인되지 않은 단계다. 투자자 입장에서는 다가오는 분기 실적 발표와 신사업의 매출 연계 여부, 자사주 신탁계약의 종료 결과를 순차적으로 확인하는 것이 중요해 보인다. 본 리포트는 공시된 사실관계 전달을 목적으로 한다.", "en": "Egis faces a profitability recovery challenge, having posted a 29.8% revenue decline and a swing to an operating loss in 2025, followed by consecutive operating losses in Q1 and Q2 of 2026. At the same time, the company is attempting changes on both the business and capital fronts, including the SaaS-based digital twin contract with Jeju Province, new businesses in physical AI and aerospace, and a KRW 3 billion treasury stock acquisition and planned cancellation. While the debt ratio has declined, operating cash flow turned to an outflow, producing diverging signals between balance-sheet structure and cash generation capacity. Given the revenue structure's heavy reliance on construction services for public institutions, quarterly volatility may persist, and the actual results of the SaaS transition have not yet been confirmed in the numbers. For readers, it appears important to sequentially track the upcoming quarterly earnings releases, whether new businesses translate into revenue, and the outcome of the treasury stock trust agreement upon its expiration. This report is intended to convey disclosed factual information."}}}
===JSON_END===

950220-05f34ec6a3915ebc9a6aeed8.text:
===JSON_START===
{"0": "In August 2026, through a contract with Tolerance Bio, the company transferred the North America, Latin America, and Europe rights for NT-I7's thymic dysfunction indication and secured a milestone structure of up to $260 million (approximately KRW 366.9 billion). The company retains the rights to core areas such as immuno-oncology, leaving room for additional partnerships. This can be interpreted as the first tangible outcome of the partnership discussions the company has continued to pursue with multiple global pharmaceutical companies.", "1": "Endari, in-licensed from Emmaus Life Sciences, is an asset that can recognize sales immediately without clinical or approval risk, and contributed to quarterly sales increasing for three consecutive quarters since the license became effective in May 2026. It is also positive that the company was able to reduce the initial sales gap by inheriting existing distribution infrastructure, including major U.S. wholesaler networks and listings with the three major PBMs.", "2": "Both operating losses and net losses attributable to controlling shareholders showed a trend of annual reduction from 2022 to 2025, and in Q2 2026, the net loss attributable to controlling shareholders continued to decrease compared to the same period of the previous year. Favorable response rates and safety reported in early data from the CAR-T combination trial are also serving as a basis for further partnership discussions.", "3": "With multiple company-led clinical trials, including the Phase 2 trial for non-small cell lung cancer (NIT-119), being voluntarily withdrawn, the clinical trials currently directly controlled by the company have been narrowed down to the solid tumor Phase 1b/2a trial and the ARS program. It is also pointed out that the CAR-T combination therapy, the core growth axis, is being conducted as an investigator-initiated trial (IIT), limiting the company's direct control.", "4": "With 2025 sales amounting to only KRW 92.31 million, the company continues to fall significantly short of the annual sales requirement of KRW 3 billion for maintaining listing. Caution from an investor protection perspective is needed, as new regulations designating penny stocks as administrative issues will take effect from July 2026, and the company was also designated as an investment alert stock in August 2026 due to a sharp stock price surge.", "5": "Endari's U.S. sales have shown a declining trend due to generic competition following patent expiration, and the license agreement includes a condition that exclusive rights convert to non-exclusive if the annual minimum sales requirement is not met. Royalty and cost margin payment obligations amounting to double-digit percentages of sales could also be a burden on profitability.", "6": "Amid the continued failure to meet the annual sales requirement of KRW 3 billion, a regulation effective from July 2026 designates stocks as administrative issues if the closing price remains below KRW 1,000 for 30 consecutive trading days. Attention should be paid to institutional risks related to trading, as the company was also designated as an investment alert stock in August 2026 due to a stock price surge.", "7": "There is a history of multiple company-led clinical trials being voluntarily withdrawn, and the CAR-T combination therapy, the core growth axis, is being conducted as an investigator-initiated trial, meaning the data acquisition schedule may be dependent on the schedules of external researchers and institutions. The expected approval timing for the ARS treatment is mentioned as 2028 at the earliest, indicating that considerable time will be needed before commercialization.", "8": "Approximately KRW 10 billion in convertible bonds remain outstanding, raising the possibility of dilution upon conversion to shares, and the company has a history of raising capital through a large-scale rights offering in 2025. The clause converting Endari's license agreement to non-exclusive if the minimum sales requirement is not met could also serve as a variable in financial performance.", "9": "NeoImmuneTech reached a turning point in 2026 with quarterly sales increasing for three consecutive quarters due to the recognition of Endari sales and the technology transfer agreement with Tolerance Bio, but 2025 annual sales amounted to only KRW 92.31 million, still far from the listing maintenance requirement. Operating losses and net losses attributable to controlling shareholders showed a trend of annual reduction from 2022 to 2025, and this trend continued in Q2 2026, but the cumulative net loss attributable to controlling shareholders over the most recent four quarters was KRW 23.5 billion, indicating that the deficit structure itself persists. For the core pipeline NT-I7, company-led clinical trials have been narrowed down to one solid tumor trial and the ARS program, while the CAR-T combination therapy relies on an investigator-initiated trial structure. Endari is an asset that can recognize sales immediately, but it carries conditional risks including a declining U.S. sales trend after patent expiration and a minimum sales requirement. Institutional variables related to trading, such as the penny stock administrative issue designation regulation and the history of investment alert stock designation, also need to be examined. In summary, this is judged to be a phase where positive signals from technology transfer and securing a commercialization asset coexist with the listing maintenance sales requirement and pipeline concentration risk."}
===JSON_END===

